### J1.3 — Request collection
### VS Code (REST Client / Humao extension), JetBrains Rider and Visual Studio 2022+ run this file directly.
### Start the app first:  dotnet run -- J1.3            (for the HTTPS experiments:  dotnet run -- J1.3 --https)
### Requests are separated by ###; run them with "Send Request" / the green arrow. See the RAW request in the server console.

@host = http://localhost:5080
@secureHost = https://localhost:5443

### 1) The simplest GET — the server writes back the raw request it saw
GET {{host}}/hello?name=dotnet&lang=en
Accept: text/plain
X-Demo: hello

### 2) POST + JSON body — note the Content-Type and Content-Length headers
POST {{host}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "product": "book",
  "quantity": 2
}

### 3) Status code families — 2xx / 3xx / 4xx / 5xx
GET {{host}}/status/200

###
GET {{host}}/status/404

###
GET {{host}}/status/503

### 4) Redirect: 302 (temporary) and 301 (permanent) — inspect the Location header
GET {{host}}/redirect

###
GET {{host}}/redirect-permanent

### 5) Idempotency: POST 3 times → the counter goes up by 3 (NOT idempotent)
POST {{host}}/counter/increment

###
POST {{host}}/counter/increment

###
GET {{host}}/counter

### 5b) PUT 3 times → the result is always the same (idempotent)
PUT {{host}}/counter/42

###
PUT {{host}}/counter/42

###
GET {{host}}/counter

### 6) Cookie: set it first, then read it (this client stores the cookie; with curl you need -c/-b)
GET {{host}}/cookie/set

###
GET {{host}}/cookie/read

### 7) Conditional GET: paste the ETag value from the response into the If-None-Match below → 304 Not Modified
GET {{host}}/cache/etag

###
GET {{host}}/cache/etag
If-None-Match: "PASTE-ETAG-HERE"

### 8) Simulate the CORS preflight by hand (the OPTIONS request the browser sends)
OPTIONS {{host}}/cors/data
Origin: http://localhost:3000
Access-Control-Request-Method: PUT
Access-Control-Request-Headers: content-type

### 8b) Disallowed origin → there is NO Access-Control-Allow-Origin in the response (the server processes the request, the BROWSER does the BLOCKING)
GET {{host}}/cors/data
Origin: http://evil.example

### 9) HTTPS (requires dotnet run -- J1.3 --https) — the response carries the Strict-Transport-Security (HSTS) header
GET {{secureHost}}/hello
